Subject: [PATCH 0/3] iommu/vsi: fix vsi_iommu_probe() error paths

Three independent error-path defects in vsi_iommu_probe(), found by
source inspection while forward-porting the RK3588 vendor media stack
against this driver. Each is self-contained:

  1. a real ioremap error is replaced by -ENOMEM, which also discards
     -EPROBE_DEFER;
  2. a platform_get_irq() failure returns without unwinding the clocks
     prepared a few lines earlier, while the very next failure path
     already unwinds them correctly; and
  3. the dma_set_mask_and_coherent() return value is discarded.

I have not been able to trigger any of these on hardware: they are probe
failure paths that a working RK3588 board does not take. The series is
compile-tested only, arm64 defconfig with CONFIG_VSI_IOMMU=y and W=1,
zero warnings, on top of b4f6d7b19f3a. Reviewing these as code rather
than as a bug report is the intent; if you would rather see the IRQ
unwind proven by fault injection before taking it, say so and I will
send that separately.

There is a fourth candidate I have deliberately left out: the hardirq
handler calls pm_runtime_resume_and_get() without pm_runtime_irq_safe().
I have not reproduced it under CONFIG_DEBUG_ATOMIC_SLEEP, so I am not
sending it as a fix.

Tool disclosure, per Documentation/process/generated-content.rst.
This series was produced with an AI coding assistant (Claude, model
claude-fable-5), and its involvement covers detection, the code
changes, and these changelogs, so I am describing all three rather
than only the code.

I was auditing this driver while forward-porting the RK3588 vendor
media stack, and asked the assistant to review vsi_iommu_probe()'s
error paths for mismatched unwind and discarded return values. It
identified the three defects below, wrote the one- and three-line
changes, and drafted the changelogs and this cover letter. I then
checked each finding against the source myself -- that the
err_unprepare_clocks label already exists and is used by the adjacent
failure path, that devm_platform_ioremap_resource() returns a
meaningful ERR_PTR, and that nothing else consumes the discarded DMA
mask return -- and I edited the result. Testing was the checkpatch and
compile run described above, which I ran; no tool wrote or ran tests.

I understand each of the three changes and can defend them in review.
Per Documentation/process/coding-assistants.rst each patch carries an
Assisted-by: trailer, and the Signed-off-by is mine alone.

Yi Ding (3):
  iommu/vsi: propagate the register mapping error from probe
  iommu/vsi: unwind prepared clocks when the interrupt is unavailable
  iommu/vsi: check that the DMA mask was applied

